ments [:clinical-documents], :get-problem-list [:problems-diagnoses], :get-medications [:medications], :get-encounter-timeline [:encounter-timeline], :get-user-context [:acl-groups :current-user-profile :role-hints :user-session-context]}, :correlation {:event-log {:current "Operational observability events are SQL-backed in mod_clinical_copilot_observability_event via CopilotObservability::recordEvent. Threads, messages, source registry rows, model metadata events, workflow-step rows, workflow-finished rows, and tool-call rows now share correlation_id where the chat path provides one.", :implication "The useful join key is now correlation_id: one chat request can be followed across API response, thread messages, model logging metadata, workflow events, and our ClinicalToolFactory tool-call events."}, :current-status ["/api/copilot/chat mints a correlation_id and returns it on success and error." "CopilotAgentService accepts the correlation_id, starts the trace with it, and attaches it transiently to ClinicalThread." "ClinicalAgentRunner stores correlation_id on user and assistant messages and passes it to ModelLog metadata." "ClinicalToolFactory wraps tool handler invocation and writes metadata-only tool-call events with tool_name, status, duration_ms, thread_id, created_by, workflow, and correlation_id." "ClinicalTools passes thread/correlation/workflow context into patient evidence tools and user-context tools." "The dashboard now counts actual SQL tool-call rows instead of relying on workflow summary metadata."], :known-gaps ["Retrieval internals are not yet broken down per FHIR/native resource with correlation_id timings." "Neuron internals remain opaque except where execution reaches our ClinicalToolFactory handlers." "Token usage is still mostly null." "Verification substeps are still coarse; citation/boundary/uncertainty/constraint checks are not each first-class observability rows." "The UI does not yet display a friendly failure/debug handle, even though t