ecide relevance or permissions." ""] ["Freeze accepted tool groups: create product/evidence-catalog/tool_groups.edn as the deterministic contract between catalog entries, topics, constraints, and tools." ""] ["Write one toy tool: implement a bounded get_patient_evidence dispatcher over accepted topics, patient/date/count constraints, purpose, and source registry output." ""] ["Build the first chat slice: add a constrained Ask Copilot path that calls get_patient_evidence, asks for cited lines, validates citations, renders source-linked output, and logs observability." ""] ["Keep verification and observability non-negotiable: every answer has citation validation, every tool call logs correlation id, patient/user ids, topics, purpose, sources read, latency, success/failure, and verification result." ""]], :tool-design-catalog {:recommended-artifact-shape {:version 1, :boundary-inputs ["pca-boundary.edn" "uca-boundary.edn"], :capabilities []}, :purpose "A tool-design catalog maps user-facing evidence capabilities to concrete PCA/UCA retrieval paths so tools can hide FHIR/table/PHP shapes from the calling model.", :steps [["Tighten :output-contract into a real small vocabulary." ""] ["Decide which capabilities collapse into one tool vs one tool per capability." ""] ["Generate a tools.edn or tool-specs.edn from capabilities.edn." ""] ["Implement one boring executor, probably :lab-evidence or :clinical-notes." ""] ["Give the CCP agent only the model-facing tool schema, not the retrieval paths." ""]], :faithfulness-rule "Every PCA/UCA retrieval surface must appear in at least one capability retrieval path.", :invariant "One catalog entry equals one retrievable evidence capability, not one table, FHIR resource, or PHP method.", :entry-shape {:id "keyword capability id", :public-meaning "human/tool meaning", :available-to-model-as "short model-facing phrase", :tool-topic "keyword topic", :retrieval-paths [], :output-contract "contract keyword or shape", :constraints {}, :sour