{:at 1789883945125, :command {:op :dissoc, :path [], :key :hello}, :result {:correlation {:event-log {:current "Operational observability events are SQL-backed in mod_clinical_copilot_observability_event via CopilotObservability::recordEvent. Threads, messages, source registry rows, model metadata events, workflow-step rows, workflow-finished rows, and tool-call rows now share correlation_id where the chat path provides one.", :implication "The useful join key is now correlation_id: one chat request can be followed across API response, thread messages, model logging metadata, workflow events, and our ClinicalToolFactory tool-call events."}, :current-status ["/api/copilot/chat mints a correlation_id and returns it on success and error." "CopilotAgentService accepts the correlation_id, starts the trace with it, and attaches it transiently to ClinicalThread." "ClinicalAgentRunner stores correlation_id on user and assistant messages and passes it to ModelLog metadata." "ClinicalToolFactory wraps tool handler invocation and writes metadata-only tool-call events with tool_name, status, duration_ms, thread_id, created_by, workflow, and correlation_id." "ClinicalTools passes thread/correlation/workflow context into patient evidence tools and user-context tools." "The dashboard now counts actual SQL tool-call rows instead of relying on workflow summary metadata."], :known-gaps ["Retrieval internals are not yet broken down per FHIR/native resource with correlation_id timings." "Neuron internals remain opaque except where execution reaches our ClinicalToolFactory handlers." "Token usage is still mostly null." "Verification substeps are still coarse; citation/boundary/uncertainty/constraint checks are not each first-class observability rows." "The UI does not yet display a friendly failure/debug handle, even though the chat API returns one." "There is no retention/cleanup policy for observability rows yet."], :predicted-problems ["A failed tool now has a tool-call row, but failures inside retrievers may still need better resource-level names to be pleasant to debug." "Tool-call counting only covers tools created through ClinicalToolFactory." "Without a UI-visible correlation handle, support/debugging still depends on inspecting raw API responses or logs." "The event table may grow indefinitely until retention is added." "Error-message redaction is intentionally blunt and may remove details useful for debugging."], :next-useful-step "Expose the returned correlation_id in the chat UI on errors, then add resource-level retrieval events only if debugging proves too murky."}, :PCA-scaffold [["Keep PCA as a compatibility wrapper that continues returning the current context envelope." ""] ["Extract or formalize the reusable policy gateway, likely by making PatientContextPolicy the shared gate rather than inventing a new one." ""] ["Extract data retrieval beneath PCA into something like PatientEvidenceRetriever, returning source-attached records without the old PCA envelope." ""] ["Make PCA call the retriever while preserving existing endpoint behavior." ""] ["Build tools on the retriever plus policy gateway, projecting results into capability-shaped output contracts instead of PCA context shape." ""] ["Move hospital course and overnight workflows onto the retriever plus policy gateway with workflow-specific projection glue." ""] ["Only then decide whether PCA dies; ideally PCA becomes either a legacy context-envelope adapter or disappears because nothing needs the old envelope." ""]], :long-term-goal "Build a source-linked, patient-scoped agentic chat tool layer where the model can choose among bounded evidence tools by topic, retrieve PCA/UCA-derived context, and answer through the existing citation verification path.", :clarifying-design [{:question "Entrypoint: new /api/copilot/chat endpoint, or replace/extend CopilotAgentService::ask?", :answer "Replace/extend. Open question: note any strong reason to keep a separate endpoint/service path."} {:question "Patient binding: should every agent chat require patient_id and encounter_id?", :answer "Yes. Agent chat should be patient- and encounter-bound."} {:question "Conversation memory: stateless per request, or persisted thread_id history?", :answer "We will need conversation."} {:question "Response mode: blocking JSON first, or streaming from day one?", :answer "Blocking for now. Streaming has a place, especially in diagnosis, but is a distraction right now and can be added later."} {:question "Tool approval: use Neuron ToolApproval middleware or skip because tools are read-only and policy-gated?", :answer "Skip Neuron approval for now. We worked hard on our own policy gates and should use them; keep Neuron at arm's length."} {:question "Tool choice: all tools available, or constrain by workflow/context?", :answer "All tools for now. Constraining by workflow/context likely adds complexity."} {:question "Output contract to UI: final text only, or text plus structured sources/citations/tool results?", :answer "Each thread needs a source registry or similar. Each tool call gives the agent sources and references; the agent returns references; references are deterministically linked back to evidence."} {:question "System prompt: general chart chat, or answer only from source-linked tool evidence?", :answer "Not a huge concern yet."}], "todos" [], :plan [["Finish the catalog seed: read product/evidence-catalog/pca-boundary.edn, join it with lay-of-the-land.edn, and emit deterministic catalog.edn." ""] ["Add UCA to the boundary: normalize UserContextAssembler into the same source catalog shape, keeping user context separate from patient evidence." ""] ["Assign topics: use the topic-assignment prompt to label catalog entries for planner-facing retrieval themes without letting the model decide relevance or permissions." ""] ["Freeze accepted tool groups: create product/evidence-catalog/tool_groups.edn as the deterministic contract between catalog entries, topics, constraints, and tools." ""] ["Write one toy tool: implement a bounded get_patient_evidence dispatcher over accepted topics, patient/date/count constraints, purpose, and source registry output." ""] ["Build the first chat slice: add a constrained Ask Copilot path that calls get_patient_evidence, asks for cited lines, validates citations, renders source-linked output, and logs observability." ""] ["Keep verification and observability non-negotiable: every answer has citation validation, every tool call logs correlation id, patient/user ids, topics, purpose, sources read, latency, success/failure, and verification result." ""]], :tool-design-catalog {:recommended-artifact-shape {:version 1, :boundary-inputs ["pca-boundary.edn" "uca-boundary.edn"], :capabilities []}, :purpose "A tool-design catalog maps user-facing evidence capabilities to concrete PCA/UCA retrieval paths so tools can hide FHIR/table/PHP shapes from the calling model.", :steps [["Tighten :output-contract into a real small vocabulary." ""] ["Decide which capabilities collapse into one tool vs one tool per capability." ""] ["Generate a tools.edn or tool-specs.edn from capabilities.edn." ""] ["Implement one boring executor, probably :lab-evidence or :clinical-notes." ""] ["Give the CCP agent only the model-facing tool schema, not the retrieval paths." ""]], :faithfulness-rule "Every PCA/UCA retrieval surface must appear in at least one capability retrieval path.", :invariant "One catalog entry equals one retrievable evidence capability, not one table, FHIR resource, or PHP method.", :entry-shape {:id "keyword capability id", :public-meaning "human/tool meaning", :available-to-model-as "short model-facing phrase", :tool-topic "keyword topic", :retrieval-paths [], :output-contract "contract keyword or shape", :constraints {}, :sources []}, :problem-with-pca-boundary "pca-boundary.edn is a useful boundary ledger but mixes resources, native add-ons, and raw tables; treat it as input coverage, not the final cata