{:at 1789884897668, :command {:op :dissoc, :path [], :key :clarifying-design}, :result {:todos ["model-as-judge-verification: revisit ClinicalBoundaryPolicy, ClinicalConstraintPolicy, and uncertainty handling; deterministic substring/regex checks are uncomfortable placeholders, and the preferred direction is a model-judge verifier with documented limits."], :correlation {:event-log {:current "Operational observability events are SQL-backed in mod_clinical_copilot_observability_event via CopilotObservability::recordEvent. Threads, messages, source registry rows, model metadata events, workflow-step rows, workflow-finished rows, and tool-call rows now share correlation_id where the chat path provides one.", :implication "The useful join key is now correlation_id: one chat request can be followed across API response, thread messages, model logging metadata, workflow events, and our ClinicalToolFactory tool-call events."}, :current-status ["/api/copilot/chat mints a correlation_id and returns it on success and error." "CopilotAgentService accepts the correlation_id, starts the trace with it, and attaches it transiently to ClinicalThread." "ClinicalAgentRunner stores correlation_id on user and assistant messages and passes it to ModelLog metadata." "ClinicalToolFactory wraps tool handler invocation and writes metadata-only tool-call events with tool_name, status, duration_ms, thread_id, created_by, workflow, and correlation_id." "ClinicalTools passes thread/correlation/workflow context into patient evidence tools and user-context tools." "The dashboard now counts actual SQL tool-call rows instead of relying on workflow summary metadata."], :known-gaps ["Retrieval internals are not yet broken down per FHIR/native resource with correlation_id timings." "Neuron internals remain opaque except where execution reaches our ClinicalToolFactory handlers." "Token usage is still mostly null." "Verification substeps are still coarse; citation/boundary/uncertainty/constraint checks are not each first-class observability rows." "The UI does not yet display a friendly failure/debug handle, even though the chat API returns one." "There is no retention/cleanup policy for observability rows yet."], :predicted-problems ["A failed tool now has a tool-call row, but failures inside retrievers may still need better resource-level names to be pleasant to debug." "Tool-call counting only covers tools created through ClinicalToolFactory." "Without a UI-visible correlation handle, support/debugging still depends on inspecting raw API responses or logs." "The event table may grow indefinitely until retention is added." "Error-message redaction is intentionally blunt and may remove details useful for debugging."], :next-useful-step "Expose the returned correlation_id in the chat UI on errors, then add resource-level retrieval events only if debugging proves too murky."}, :long-term-goal "Build a source-linked, patient-scoped agentic chat tool layer where the model can choose among bounded evidence tools by topic, retrieve PCA/UCA-derived context, and answer through the existing citation verification path.", "todos" [], :plan [["Finish the catalog seed: read product/evidence-catalog/pca-boundary.edn, join it with lay-of-the-land.edn, and emit deterministic catalog.edn." ""] ["Add UCA to the boundary: normalize UserContextAssembler into the same source catalog shape, keeping user context separate from patient evidence." ""] ["Assign topics: use the topic-assignment prompt to label catalog entries for planner-facing retrieval themes without letting the model decide relevance or permissions." ""] ["Freeze accepted tool groups: create product/evidence-catalog/tool_groups.edn as the deterministic contract between catalog entries, topics, constraints, and tools." ""] ["Write one toy tool: implement a bounded get_patient_evidence dispatcher over accepted topics, patient/date/count constraints, purpose, and source registry output." ""] ["Build the first chat slice: add a constrained Ask Copilot path that calls get_patient_evidence, asks for cited lines, validates citations, renders source-linked output, and logs observability." ""] ["Keep verification and observability non-negotiable: every answer has citation validation, every tool call logs correlation id, patient/user ids, topics, purpose, sources read, latency, success/failure, and verification result." ""]], :short-term-goal "Create the first automated evidence-catalog pipeline from pca-boundary.edn to deterministic catalog.edn, then derive a tiny tool_groups.edn contract from that catalog."}, :before {:op :dissoc, :path [], :key :clarifying-design, :existed? true, :old [{:question "Entrypoint: new /api/copilot/chat endpoint, or replace/extend CopilotAgentService::ask?", :answer "Replace/extend. Open question: note any strong reason to keep a separate endpoint/service path."} {:question "Patient binding: should every agent chat require patient_id and encounter_id?", :answer "Yes. Agent chat should be patient- and encounter-bound."} {:question "Conversation memory: stateless per request, or persisted thread_id history?", :answer "We will need conversation."} {:question "Response mode: blocking JSON first, or streaming from day one?", :answer "Blocking for now. Streaming has a place, especially in diagnosis, but is a distraction right now and can be added later."} {:question "Tool approval: use Neuron ToolApproval middleware or skip because tools are read-only and policy-gated?", :answer "Skip Neuron approval for now. We worked hard on our own policy gates and should use them; keep Neuron at arm's length."} {:question "Tool choice: all tools available, or constrain by workflow/context?", :answer "All tools for now. Constraining by workflow/context likely adds complexity."} {:question "Output contract to UI: final text only, or text plus structured sources/citations/tool results?", :answer "Each thread needs a source registry or similar. Each tool call gives the agent sources and references; the agent returns references; references are deterministically linked back to evidence."} {:question "System prompt: general chart chat, or answer only from source-linked tool evidence?", :answer "Not a huge concern yet."}]}}
